Subject: Give a cost to right brackets that an ERROR node does not match

Give a cost to each right bracket that has no left bracket in an ERROR node.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
ef148db.

After a syntax error, GCC and Clang skip tokens, and they stop before a
right bracket if they did not skip its left bracket
(cp_parser_skip_to_end_of_statement in gcc/cp/parser.cc, Parser::SkipUntil
in clang/lib/Parse/Parser.cpp). The error costs of the runtime did not
agree. To skip a right brace cost 101. The construct of the brace then
stayed open until the end of the file or of the include guard. There,
error recovery put the full construct into one ERROR node.

An ERROR node now records its brackets that have no match in the node.
Each right brace with no left brace costs 10000. Each right parenthesis
or square bracket with no left one costs 1000. The skip of a token
includes this cost before the parser keeps the version. The products of
ts_parser__compare_versions use 64 bits. The larger costs then do not
overflow.

On the corpus at e944ebb, the ERROR bytes go from 32.72 MB to 11.76 MB.
The files with an ERROR over 90% of the file go from 338 to 96. No file
without an error changes. A benchmark puts one error into each of 4,000
files without an error. For errors that keep the brackets balanced, the
named nodes outside the edit that change go from 22,647 to 17,141. For
errors that add or remove a bracket, they go from 68,241 to 63,964.

The repair reads the names of the token symbols to find the brackets. Upstream can reject a
heuristic that reads token names in the runtime of each language. An alternative gives the
bracket symbols in the language, or in a field of the parser.

The patch also adds 8 bytes to `SubtreeHeapData`.

Risk for upstream: high, because of the two points above.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

